course: dictionary
lesson: 5965
title: A leader called matriarch
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A matriarch is a woman who is the head of a family or group, often because she is the oldest and most respected. You can often find her meaning from the words around her. «An elephant family is led by its oldest female, the matriarch, who remembers water holes, paths and dangers over decades.» The word led and the words oldest female tell you that the matriarch is the one in charge.
explain: Look for the clue after the comma. «At the front walks the grandmother, the matriarch, who remembers where the water is.» The words after the comma explain who the matriarch is: the grandmother at the front. When a word is followed by a comma and more words, those words often explain it.
explain: Test your idea by putting it into the sentence. Replace matriarch with "the head of the family": «An elephant family is led by its oldest female, the head of the family.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right. The opposite of matriarch is patriarch, the male leader.
fact: A matriarch is a woman who is the head of a family or group.
fact: In animal groups, such as elephants, the matriarch is the old female who leads the herd.
fact: A matriarch is often the oldest and most respected woman in her family or group.
fact: The opposite of matriarch is patriarch.
fact: Context clue: words after a comma, like «the grandmother, the matriarch», often explain a hard word.
exercise: «An elephant family is led by its oldest female, the matriarch.» What is a matriarch? | *The head of a family or group, often the oldest and most respected | A dry, empty waterhole | A young elephant that is just learning to walk | A tall tree on the plain
exercise: «In a drought, the matriarch remembers a waterhole the herd hasn't visited for years.» In an elephant herd, who is the matriarch? | *The old female who leads the herd | The youngest baby elephant | A grown-up male who leaves the herd | The rain that falls in the drought
exercise: Which word is the opposite of matriarch? | Herd | *Patriarch | Baby | Waterhole
test: «At the front walks the grandmother, the matriarch, who remembers where the water is.» What does matriarch mean here? | The baby walking at the back | *The grandmother at the front, who knows where the water is | The river that runs past the herd | The man who leaves the herd as a teenager
test: Nan has done the family drive for fifty years and knows every road. Which word fits? Nan is the family's ___. | *Matriarch | Waterhole | Stranger | Baby
exam: Why does the elephant herd follow the matriarch? | Because she is the only one who can swim | *Because she has lived longest and remembers the most | Because she carries all the food | Because she is the smallest and youngest
